{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TxhbreBSbDL3AGJhFE9F6e","type":"tool_result","content":"6. `result.go` (new): `swap` (rename `<id>` to `<id>.input`, `<id>.result/work` to `<id>`, then `<id>.done` with `O_EXCL` 0600 and fsync of the dir); each step re-checkable after a crash.\n7. `watch.go` (new): per-job goroutine polling `GetPod` every 2s; revoke token once when `pre` terminates; map pre failures, pull back-off, unschedulable for 5m, eviction, `DeadlineExceeded` to `.done` with `End`; after `agent` terminates, pull the result from the pod IP with the bearer key, retry 409/429/5xx/network until `Deadline+ResultGrace`, a fresh `<id>.result` per attempt, `tarball.Unpack`; `EndBadResult` with no retry; verify pod UID unchanged before pulling; copy `out/stdout` to `h.StdoutPath`. Use `HTTP` and `Now` options for tests. Sanitise and cap termination messages.\n8. `kube.go`: `Start` (refuse `Stdin`, `Policy` checks, config-dir Fixed must equal `jobpod.AgentConfig`, `ErrNotPrepared`, set `Deadline`, mint token for job and sidecar repos, `jobpod.NewKey`, `CreatePod` then owner-referenced `CreateSecret`, rollback with pod delete and revoke on failure, start watcher and log follower), `Status`, `Logs` (read local files as `internal/executor/local/local.go` does), `Cleanup` (idempotent; foreign Kind removes dirs only; the moved worktree is removed by directory removal then `Prune`, not `worktree remove`).\n9. `logs.go` (new): follow `PodLogs` for `agent` into `h.LogPath`, strip timestamps, reconnect from the last timestamp until the agent ends.\n10. `kube.go` or `sweep.go` (new): `Sweep(ctx, keep func(id string) bool)` selecting on repo and component labels; `Secrets() []string`; Reaper kill path goes through `Cleanup`.\n11. `docs/layout.md`: replace the `internal/executor/kube/` mention so it lists the executor files; keep the `api/` line.\n12. Run `make lint test`. If the diff passes about 1,500 lines, split steps 9 and 10 into a follow-up as the issue says.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make lint test` (or `go test ./internal/executor/...`). All tests use `api/fake` and `httptest`; no network or cluster.\n- `TestBuildPod` (`pod_test.go`), table: plain, ReadOnly, sidecar, history, API key vs OAuth. Expect: agent has no Secret volume and no token or key in env; only `pre` mounts the token item and only `post` the result key; security contexts match the ops notes; deadlines; name <= 63; labels valid label values.\n- `TestMapStatus` (`status_test.go`): one case per row of the table, plus foreign Kind and missing worktree.\n- `TestLifecycle` (`kube_test.go`): Prepare, Start, pre terminated (token revoked once), agent exit 3, pull, `Exited` with code 3, worktree swapped, stdout copied.\n- `TestPull` (`watch_test.go`), table: 409 twice then 200; unsafe tar gives `EndBadResult` with no retry; over limit; deadline gives `EndNoResult`; pod UID changed is not pulled.\n- `TestEnds`: eviction, image pull back-off, unschedulable timeout, pre exit 3 and 1, `DeadlineExceeded` gives 124 and `TimedOut`.\n- `TestStartRollback` (Secret create fails: pod deleted, token revoked), `TestInputsTooLarge`, `TestStartRefusals` (Stdin, bad config-dir, not prepared, ID too long, no RoleSource), `TestOrphanAfterRestart`, `TestCleanupIdempotent` (including KeepWorktree and foreign Kind), `TestSweep` (another repo's pods untouched), `TestLogFollowReconnect`, `TestSwapCrashResume`.\n- Run with `-race`.\n\n### Risk\n\nHigh. A state machine across the controller, kubelet and pod, with credentials (read token, result key, model credential) and HTTP pull of untrusted tar content. Mitigated by pure `buildPod` and `mapStatus`, the unpack limits in `internal/tarball`, and the fake. No protected path is touched (`docs/layout.md` and `internal/` are not in `merge.protected_paths`); no `deploy/` change. The change widens the `executor` public types (`Status.End`, `Job.RoleSource`); `local` must keep behaving identically. Concurrency: one watcher goroutine per job and a shared `live` map; needs `-race`.\n\n### Size\n\nL, about 1,300 lines (roughly 700 code, 600 tests), within the 3,000-line worker block limit. Files: `internal/executor/executor.go`, `internal/executor/errors.go`, `internal/executor/kube/{kube,pod,status,result,watch,logs}.go` and their `_test.go` files (all new), `docs/layout.md`.\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds the Kubernetes executor in `internal/executor/kube`: it builds the job pod and Secret, watches the pod, pulls the result archive back from the post container, maps pod state to executor status, follows logs, and cleans up and sweeps. The shared types it needs are added to `internal/executor`.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/executor`: `Job.RoleSource`, `Status.End` with the five `End*` constants, `ErrInputsTooLarge`.\n- `kube/kube.go`: `Tokens`, `Options`, `New`, Prepare, Start (with rollback), Status, Logs, idempotent Cleanup, `Sweep`, `Secrets`.\n- `kube/pod.go`: pure `buildPod` and `buildSecret`. Pre and post get separate Secret volumes, so only pre mounts the token and only post mounts the result key. The agent gets the credential only as a `secretKeyRef`.\n- `kube/status.go`: pure `mapStatus`. `kube/result.go`: crash-resumable `swap` and the `.done` marker. `kube/watch.go`: poller, result pull, end mapping. `kube/logs.go`: log follower.\n- `kube/api`: `FSGroupChangePolicy` field; the fake gains `SetInitContainer` and `Mutate`.\n- `docs/layout.md`: the new package line.\n\n## Testing\n`go vet ./internal/executor/...` and `go test -race ./internal/executor/...` pass, including `-count=5` on the kube package. gofmt is clean on the changed files. Tests use `api/fake` and an httptest server only: TestBuildPod, TestBuildSecret, TestMapStatus, TestLifecycle, TestPull, TestEnds, TestStartRollback, TestInputsTooLarge, TestPrepareRefusals, TestStartRefusals, TestOrphanAfterRestart, TestCleanupIdempotent, TestSweep, TestLogFollowReconnect, TestSwapCrashResume.\n\n## Open issues\n- `Sweep(ctx, keep)` takes the repo from a new `Options.Repo`, because the plan gave it no repo argument.\n- Network label: `NetworkAdvisory` and `NetworkNone` both map to `false`; `NetworkOn` maps to `true`.\n- After the swap, the original worktree's `.git` link is moved into the result so close-out's git calls still work. `tarball.Unpack` already refuses a `.git` entry.\n- `Status` reports a held job whose pod vanished as Running until the watcher writes the marker, so Gone carries the real End reason and not `EndNoResult`. `mapStatus` itself follows the table.\n- The pod has no scheduling condition in the API types, so \"unschedulable\" is approximated as Pending with `pre` still waiting for 5 minutes.\n- `golangci-lint` reports errcheck findings in the repo already; the repo's own `make lint` (vet and gofmt) is clean for these files.\npackage kube\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor/kube/api\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/jobpod\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball\"\n)\n\nconst maxReason = 200\n\n// sanitize makes a pod-supplied message safe to log and store: printable\n// ASCII only and capped.\nfunc sanitize(s string) string {\n\tb := make([]byte, 0, len(s))\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(s) && len(b) < maxReason; i++ {\n\t\tif c := s[i]; c >= 0x20 && c < 0x7f {\n\t\t\tb = append(b, c)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tb = append(b, '?')\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(b))\n}\n\nfunc containerState(list []api.ContainerStatus, name string) (api.ContainerState, bool) {\n\tfor _, c := range list {\n\t\tif c.Name == name {\n\t\t\treturn c.State, true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn api.ContainerState{}, false\n}\n\nfunc signalName(n int32) string {\n\tswitch n {\n\tcase 0:\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\tcase 9:\n\t\treturn \"killed\"\n\tcase 15:\n\t\treturn \"terminated\"\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"signal %d\", n)\n}\n\n// watch polls the pod until the job has ended, then leaves the .done marker.\n// It runs one goroutine per job. Once the marker is written it returns.\nfunc (e *Executor) watch(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob) {\n\tt := time.NewTicker(e.o.Poll)\n\tdefer t.Stop()\n\tfor {\n\t\tif e.step(ctx, h, lj) {\n\t\t\te.mu.Lock()\n\t\t\tlj.agentEnded.Store(true)\n\t\t\te.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tcase <-t.C:\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// end writes a marker for a job that ended without a result.\nfunc (e *Executor) end(h executor.Handle, why executor.End, reason string) bool {\n\te.o.Log.Warn(\"kube.job_ended\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"end\", string(why), \"reason\", reason)\n\treturn e.finish(h, doneFile{End: why, Reason: sanitize(reason), Finished: e.o.Now().UTC()})\n}\n\nfunc (e *Executor) finish(h executor.Handle, d doneFile) bool {\n\tif err := writeDone(h, d); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Error(\"kube.done_write_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false // try again on the next tick\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// step runs one poll and reports whether the job is finished.\nfunc (e *Executor) step(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob) bool {\n\tif !exists(h.Worktree) && !exists(h.Worktree+\".input\") {\n\t\treturn true // Cleanup removed the job's directories: nothing to record\n\t}\n\tnow := e.o.Now()\n\tpod, err := e.o.Client.GetPod(ctx, e.o.Namespace, jobpod.PodName(h.JobID))\n\tagentEnded := lj.agentEnded.Load()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase errors.Is(err, api.ErrNotFound):\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod is gone before the agent ended\")\n\tcase err != nil:\n\t\tif now.After(h.Deadline.Add(e.o.ResultGrace)) {\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndNoResult, \"pod status unavailable past the deadline\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn false\n\tcase pod.Meta.UID != lj.uid:\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod was replaced\")\n\t}\n\tst := pod.Status\n\tif s, ok := containerState(st.InitContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerPre); ok && s.Terminated != nil {\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\tif code := s.Terminated.ExitCode; code != 0 {\n\t\t\twhy := executor.EndCloneFailed\n\t\t\tif code == jobpod.ExitPermanent {\n\t\t\t\twhy = executor.EndPrepFailed\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, why, s.Terminated.Message)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\ta, haveAgent := containerState(st.ContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerAgent)\n\tif haveAgent && a.Terminated != nil {\n\t\tif !agentEnded {\n\t\t\tlj.agentEnded.Store(true)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn e.pull(ctx, h, lj, pod, a.Terminated)\n\t}\n\t// The agent has not ended.\n\tif st.Reason == \"DeadlineExceeded\" {\n\t\treturn e.finish(h, doneFile{Exit: exitTimeout, TimedOut: true, Finished: now.UTC(), Reason: \"pod deadline exceeded\"})\n\t}\n\tif st.Reason == \"Evicted\" || st.Phase == \"Failed\" || st.Phase == \"Succeeded\" {\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, firstNonEmpty(st.Message, st.Reason, \"pod \"+st.Phase))\n\t}\n\tfor _, list := range [][]api.ContainerStatus{st.InitContainerStatuses, st.ContainerStatuses} {\n\t\tfor _, c := range list {\n\t\t\tif w := c.State.Waiting; w != nil && (w.Reason == \"ErrImagePull\" || w.Reason == \"ImagePullBackOff\") {\n\t\t\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, c.Name+\": \"+w.Reason+\": \"+w.Message)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif st.Phase == \"Pending\" && now.Sub(h.StartedAt) > e.o.PendingTimeout {\n\t\tif s, ok := containerState(st.InitContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerPre); !ok || s.Waiting != nil {\n\t\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod not scheduled in time\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc firstNonEmpty(s ...string) string {\n\tfor _, v := range s {\n\t\tif v != \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn v\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n\n// pull fetches the result once. It reports true when the job is finished; a\n// retryable failure returns false and is tried again on the next poll until\n// Deadline+ResultGrace.\nfunc (e *Executor) pull(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob, pod *api.Pod, term *api.StateTerminated) bool {\n\tcut := h.Deadline.Add(e.o.ResultGrace)\n\tgive := func(reason string) bool {\n\t\tif e.o.Now().After(cut) {\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndNoResult, reason)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tip := pod.Status.PodIP\n\tif ip == \"\" {\n\t\treturn give(\"pod has no IP\")\n\t}\n\tres := h.Worktree + \".result\"\n\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\tif err := os.Mkdir(res, 0o700); err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(err.Error())\n\t}\n\tu := fmt.Sprintf(\"http://%s:%d%s\", ip, jobpod.ResultPort, jobpod.ResultPath)\n\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, u, nil)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(err.Error())\n\t}\n\treq.Header.Set(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer \"+lj.key)\n\tresp, err := e.o.HTTP.Do(req)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(\"result pull: \" + sanitize(err.Error()))\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n\tif resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n\t\tio.Copy(io.Discard, io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 4096))\n\t\treturn give(fmt.Sprintf(\"result pull: status %d\", resp.StatusCode))\n\t}\n\tif _, err := tarball.Unpack(resp.Body, res, e.o.Limits); err != nil {\n\t\tvar te *tarball.Error\n\t\tif errors.As(err, &te) {\n\t\t\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndBadResult, te.Error())\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn give(\"result pull: \" + sanitize(err.Error()))\n\t}\n\tif fi, err := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(res, jobpod.RootWork)); err != nil || !fi.IsDir() {\n\t\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndBadResult, \"result has no work tree\")\n\t}\n\tif err := copyStdout(filepath.Join(res, jobpod.RootOut, jobpod.StdoutName), h.StdoutPath); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Warn(\"kube.stdout_copy_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := swap(h); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Error(\"kube.swap_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\td := doneFile{Exit: int(term.ExitCode), Signal: signalName(term.Signal), Finished: term.FinishedAt}\n\tif term.Signal != 0 {\n\t\td.Exit = -1\n\t}\n\tif d.Finished.IsZero() {\n\t\td.Finished = e.o.Now().UTC()\n\t}\n\treturn e.finish(h, d)\n}\n\n// copyStdout copies the packed stdout file, if any. It opens src without\n// following links; the unpacked tree holds no symlink that escapes it.\nfunc copyStdout(src, dst string) error {\n\tif dst == \"\" {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tfi, err := os.Lstat(src)\n\tif err != nil || !fi.Mode().IsRegular() {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tin, err := os.Open(src)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdefer in.Close()\n\tout, err := os.OpenFile(dst, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREATE|os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\t_, cerr := io.Copy(out, in)\n\treturn errors.Join(cerr, out.Close())\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f83dc75-c2d0-4d48-85be-43f3b8d27d72","uuid":"86511971-7327-4619-bd15-e9ac94de2cf1","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13:26:35.398Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"6. `result.go` (new): `swap` (rename `<id>` to `<id>.input`, `<id>.result/work` to `<id>`, then `<id>.done` with `O_EXCL` 0600 and fsync of the dir); each step re-checkable after a crash.\n7. `watch.go` (new): per-job goroutine polling `GetPod` every 2s; revoke token once when `pre` terminates; map pre failures, pull back-off, unschedulable for 5m, eviction, `DeadlineExceeded` to `.done` with `End`; after `agent` terminates, pull the result from the pod IP with the bearer key, retry 409/429/5xx/network until `Deadline+ResultGrace`, a fresh `<id>.result` per attempt, `tarball.Unpack`; `EndBadResult` with no retry; verify pod UID unchanged before pulling; copy `out/stdout` to `h.StdoutPath`. Use `HTTP` and `Now` options for tests. Sanitise and cap termination messages.\n8. `kube.go`: `Start` (refuse `Stdin`, `Policy` checks, config-dir Fixed must equal `jobpod.AgentConfig`, `ErrNotPrepared`, set `Deadline`, mint token for job and sidecar repos, `jobpod.NewKey`, `CreatePod` then owner-referenced `CreateSecret`, rollback with pod delete and revoke on failure, start watcher and log follower), `Status`, `Logs` (read local files as `internal/executor/local/local.go` does), `Cleanup` (idempotent; foreign Kind removes dirs only; the moved worktree is removed by directory removal then `Prune`, not `worktree remove`).\n9. `logs.go` (new): follow `PodLogs` for `agent` into `h.LogPath`, strip timestamps, reconnect from the last timestamp until the agent ends.\n10. `kube.go` or `sweep.go` (new): `Sweep(ctx, keep func(id string) bool)` selecting on repo and component labels; `Secrets() []string`; Reaper kill path goes through `Cleanup`.\n11. `docs/layout.md`: replace the `internal/executor/kube/` mention so it lists the executor files; keep the `api/` line.\n12. Run `make lint test`. If the diff passes about 1,500 lines, split steps 9 and 10 into a follow-up as the issue says.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make lint test` (or `go test ./internal/executor/...`). All tests use `api/fake` and `httptest`; no network or cluster.\n- `TestBuildPod` (`pod_test.go`), table: plain, ReadOnly, sidecar, history, API key vs OAuth. Expect: agent has no Secret volume and no token or key in env; only `pre` mounts the token item and only `post` the result key; security contexts match the ops notes; deadlines; name <= 63; labels valid label values.\n- `TestMapStatus` (`status_test.go`): one case per row of the table, plus foreign Kind and missing worktree.\n- `TestLifecycle` (`kube_test.go`): Prepare, Start, pre terminated (token revoked once), agent exit 3, pull, `Exited` with code 3, worktree swapped, stdout copied.\n- `TestPull` (`watch_test.go`), table: 409 twice then 200; unsafe tar gives `EndBadResult` with no retry; over limit; deadline gives `EndNoResult`; pod UID changed is not pulled.\n- `TestEnds`: eviction, image pull back-off, unschedulable timeout, pre exit 3 and 1, `DeadlineExceeded` gives 124 and `TimedOut`.\n- `TestStartRollback` (Secret create fails: pod deleted, token revoked), `TestInputsTooLarge`, `TestStartRefusals` (Stdin, bad config-dir, not prepared, ID too long, no RoleSource), `TestOrphanAfterRestart`, `TestCleanupIdempotent` (including KeepWorktree and foreign Kind), `TestSweep` (another repo's pods untouched), `TestLogFollowReconnect`, `TestSwapCrashResume`.\n- Run with `-race`.\n\n### Risk\n\nHigh. A state machine across the controller, kubelet and pod, with credentials (read token, result key, model credential) and HTTP pull of untrusted tar content. Mitigated by pure `buildPod` and `mapStatus`, the unpack limits in `internal/tarball`, and the fake. No protected path is touched (`docs/layout.md` and `internal/` are not in `merge.protected_paths`); no `deploy/` change. The change widens the `executor` public types (`Status.End`, `Job.RoleSource`); `local` must keep behaving identically. Concurrency: one watcher goroutine per job and a shared `live` map; needs `-race`.\n\n### Size\n\nL, about 1,300 lines (roughly 700 code, 600 tests), within the 3,000-line worker block limit. Files: `internal/executor/executor.go`, `internal/executor/errors.go`, `internal/executor/kube/{kube,pod,status,result,watch,logs}.go` and their `_test.go` files (all new), `docs/layout.md`.\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds the Kubernetes executor in `internal/executor/kube`: it builds the job pod and Secret, watches the pod, pulls the result archive back from the post container, maps pod state to executor status, follows logs, and cleans up and sweeps. The shared types it needs are added to `internal/executor`.\n\n## Changes\n- `internal/executor`: `Job.RoleSource`, `Status.End` with the five `End*` constants, `ErrInputsTooLarge`.\n- `kube/kube.go`: `Tokens`, `Options`, `New`, Prepare, Start (with rollback), Status, Logs, idempotent Cleanup, `Sweep`, `Secrets`.\n- `kube/pod.go`: pure `buildPod` and `buildSecret`. Pre and post get separate Secret volumes, so only pre mounts the token and only post mounts the result key. The agent gets the credential only as a `secretKeyRef`.\n- `kube/status.go`: pure `mapStatus`. `kube/result.go`: crash-resumable `swap` and the `.done` marker. `kube/watch.go`: poller, result pull, end mapping. `kube/logs.go`: log follower.\n- `kube/api`: `FSGroupChangePolicy` field; the fake gains `SetInitContainer` and `Mutate`.\n- `docs/layout.md`: the new package line.\n\n## Testing\n`go vet ./internal/executor/...` and `go test -race ./internal/executor/...` pass, including `-count=5` on the kube package. gofmt is clean on the changed files. Tests use `api/fake` and an httptest server only: TestBuildPod, TestBuildSecret, TestMapStatus, TestLifecycle, TestPull, TestEnds, TestStartRollback, TestInputsTooLarge, TestPrepareRefusals, TestStartRefusals, TestOrphanAfterRestart, TestCleanupIdempotent, TestSweep, TestLogFollowReconnect, TestSwapCrashResume.\n\n## Open issues\n- `Sweep(ctx, keep)` takes the repo from a new `Options.Repo`, because the plan gave it no repo argument.\n- Network label: `NetworkAdvisory` and `NetworkNone` both map to `false`; `NetworkOn` maps to `true`.\n- After the swap, the original worktree's `.git` link is moved into the result so close-out's git calls still work. `tarball.Unpack` already refuses a `.git` entry.\n- `Status` reports a held job whose pod vanished as Running until the watcher writes the marker, so Gone carries the real End reason and not `EndNoResult`. `mapStatus` itself follows the table.\n- The pod has no scheduling condition in the API types, so \"unschedulable\" is approximated as Pending with `pre` still waiting for 5 minutes.\n- `golangci-lint` reports errcheck findings in the repo already; the repo's own `make lint` (vet and gofmt) is clean for these files.\npackage kube\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"net/http\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/executor/kube/api\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/jobpod\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball\"\n)\n\nconst maxReason = 200\n\n// sanitize makes a pod-supplied message safe to log and store: printable\n// ASCII only and capped.\nfunc sanitize(s string) string {\n\tb := make([]byte, 0, len(s))\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(s) && len(b) < maxReason; i++ {\n\t\tif c := s[i]; c >= 0x20 && c < 0x7f {\n\t\t\tb = append(b, c)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tb = append(b, '?')\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(b))\n}\n\nfunc containerState(list []api.ContainerStatus, name string) (api.ContainerState, bool) {\n\tfor _, c := range list {\n\t\tif c.Name == name {\n\t\t\treturn c.State, true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn api.ContainerState{}, false\n}\n\nfunc signalName(n int32) string {\n\tswitch n {\n\tcase 0:\n\t\treturn \"\"\n\tcase 9:\n\t\treturn \"killed\"\n\tcase 15:\n\t\treturn \"terminated\"\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"signal %d\", n)\n}\n\n// watch polls the pod until the job has ended, then leaves the .done marker.\n// It runs one goroutine per job. Once the marker is written it returns.\nfunc (e *Executor) watch(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob) {\n\tt := time.NewTicker(e.o.Poll)\n\tdefer t.Stop()\n\tfor {\n\t\tif e.step(ctx, h, lj) {\n\t\t\te.mu.Lock()\n\t\t\tlj.agentEnded.Store(true)\n\t\t\te.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\t}\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\t\treturn\n\t\tcase <-t.C:\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// end writes a marker for a job that ended without a result.\nfunc (e *Executor) end(h executor.Handle, why executor.End, reason string) bool {\n\te.o.Log.Warn(\"kube.job_ended\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"end\", string(why), \"reason\", reason)\n\treturn e.finish(h, doneFile{End: why, Reason: sanitize(reason), Finished: e.o.Now().UTC()})\n}\n\nfunc (e *Executor) finish(h executor.Handle, d doneFile) bool {\n\tif err := writeDone(h, d); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Error(\"kube.done_write_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false // try again on the next tick\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\n// step runs one poll and reports whether the job is finished.\nfunc (e *Executor) step(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob) bool {\n\tif !exists(h.Worktree) && !exists(h.Worktree+\".input\") {\n\t\treturn true // Cleanup removed the job's directories: nothing to record\n\t}\n\tnow := e.o.Now()\n\tpod, err := e.o.Client.GetPod(ctx, e.o.Namespace, jobpod.PodName(h.JobID))\n\tagentEnded := lj.agentEnded.Load()\n\tswitch {\n\tcase errors.Is(err, api.ErrNotFound):\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod is gone before the agent ended\")\n\tcase err != nil:\n\t\tif now.After(h.Deadline.Add(e.o.ResultGrace)) {\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndNoResult, \"pod status unavailable past the deadline\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn false\n\tcase pod.Meta.UID != lj.uid:\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod was replaced\")\n\t}\n\tst := pod.Status\n\tif s, ok := containerState(st.InitContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerPre); ok && s.Terminated != nil {\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\tif code := s.Terminated.ExitCode; code != 0 {\n\t\t\twhy := executor.EndCloneFailed\n\t\t\tif code == jobpod.ExitPermanent {\n\t\t\t\twhy = executor.EndPrepFailed\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, why, s.Terminated.Message)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\ta, haveAgent := containerState(st.ContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerAgent)\n\tif haveAgent && a.Terminated != nil {\n\t\tif !agentEnded {\n\t\t\tlj.agentEnded.Store(true)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn e.pull(ctx, h, lj, pod, a.Terminated)\n\t}\n\t// The agent has not ended.\n\tif st.Reason == \"DeadlineExceeded\" {\n\t\treturn e.finish(h, doneFile{Exit: exitTimeout, TimedOut: true, Finished: now.UTC(), Reason: \"pod deadline exceeded\"})\n\t}\n\tif st.Reason == \"Evicted\" || st.Phase == \"Failed\" || st.Phase == \"Succeeded\" {\n\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, firstNonEmpty(st.Message, st.Reason, \"pod \"+st.Phase))\n\t}\n\tfor _, list := range [][]api.ContainerStatus{st.InitContainerStatuses, st.ContainerStatuses} {\n\t\tfor _, c := range list {\n\t\t\tif w := c.State.Waiting; w != nil && (w.Reason == \"ErrImagePull\" || w.Reason == \"ImagePullBackOff\") {\n\t\t\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, c.Name+\": \"+w.Reason+\": \"+w.Message)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif st.Phase == \"Pending\" && now.Sub(h.StartedAt) > e.o.PendingTimeout {\n\t\tif s, ok := containerState(st.InitContainerStatuses, jobpod.ContainerPre); !ok || s.Waiting != nil {\n\t\t\te.revoke(ctx, lj)\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndEvicted, \"pod not scheduled in time\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\nfunc firstNonEmpty(s ...string) string {\n\tfor _, v := range s {\n\t\tif v != \"\" {\n\t\t\treturn v\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n\n// pull fetches the result once. It reports true when the job is finished; a\n// retryable failure returns false and is tried again on the next poll until\n// Deadline+ResultGrace.\nfunc (e *Executor) pull(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle, lj *liveJob, pod *api.Pod, term *api.StateTerminated) bool {\n\tcut := h.Deadline.Add(e.o.ResultGrace)\n\tgive := func(reason string) bool {\n\t\tif e.o.Now().After(cut) {\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndNoResult, reason)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tip := pod.Status.PodIP\n\tif ip == \"\" {\n\t\treturn give(\"pod has no IP\")\n\t}\n\tres := h.Worktree + \".result\"\n\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\tif err := os.Mkdir(res, 0o700); err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(err.Error())\n\t}\n\tu := fmt.Sprintf(\"http://%s:%d%s\", ip, jobpod.ResultPort, jobpod.ResultPath)\n\treq, err := http.NewRequestWithContext(ctx, http.MethodGet, u, nil)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(err.Error())\n\t}\n\treq.Header.Set(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer \"+lj.key)\n\tresp, err := e.o.HTTP.Do(req)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn give(\"result pull: \" + sanitize(err.Error()))\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()\n\tif resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {\n\t\tio.Copy(io.Discard, io.LimitReader(resp.Body, 4096))\n\t\treturn give(fmt.Sprintf(\"result pull: status %d\", resp.StatusCode))\n\t}\n\tif _, err := tarball.Unpack(resp.Body, res, e.o.Limits); err != nil {\n\t\tvar te *tarball.Error\n\t\tif errors.As(err, &te) {\n\t\t\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\t\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndBadResult, te.Error())\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn give(\"result pull: \" + sanitize(err.Error()))\n\t}\n\tif fi, err := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(res, jobpod.RootWork)); err != nil || !fi.IsDir() {\n\t\tos.RemoveAll(res)\n\t\treturn e.end(h, executor.EndBadResult, \"result has no work tree\")\n\t}\n\tif err := copyStdout(filepath.Join(res, jobpod.RootOut, jobpod.StdoutName), h.StdoutPath); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Warn(\"kube.stdout_copy_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := swap(h); err != nil {\n\t\te.o.Log.Error(\"kube.swap_failed\", \"job\", h.JobID, \"err\", err)\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\td := doneFile{Exit: int(term.ExitCode), Signal: signalName(term.Signal), Finished: term.FinishedAt}\n\tif term.Signal != 0 {\n\t\td.Exit = -1\n\t}\n\tif d.Finished.IsZero() {\n\t\td.Finished = e.o.Now().UTC()\n\t}\n\treturn e.finish(h, d)\n}\n\n// copyStdout copies the packed stdout file, if any. It opens src without\n// following links; the unpacked tree holds no symlink that escapes it.\nfunc copyStdout(src, dst string) error {\n\tif dst == \"\" {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tfi, err := os.Lstat(src)\n\tif err != nil || !fi.Mode().IsRegular() {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tin, err := os.Open(src)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tdefer in.Close()\n\tout, err := os.OpenFile(dst, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREATE|os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\t_, cerr := io.Copy(out, in)\n\treturn errors.Join(cerr, out.Close())\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}